-- title:
--   Cyclotomic discrete valuation ring mapping to a local domain
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 3$, and let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain of characteristic zero and a local ring, whose residue field $R/\mathfrak m_R$ has characteristic $q$. Let $\zeta \in R$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, in the sense that $\zeta^q = 1$ and $q$ divides every $l$ with $\zeta^l = 1$. The assertion is that there exist a type $A$ carrying the structure of a commutative ring which is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring whose residue field $A/\mathfrak m_A$ is finite, an element $\varpi \in A$ generating the maximal ideal, i.e. $\mathfrak m_A = (\varpi)$, an element $\varepsilon \in A$ which is a unit, such that $\varpi^{\,q-1} = \varepsilon \cdot q$ in $A$ (the exponent being the truncated subtraction $q - 1$ in $\mathbb N$), and a ring homomorphism $\iota : A \to R$ which is local (the preimage of $\mathfrak m_R$ is contained in $\mathfrak m_A$, equivalently $\iota(\mathfrak m_A) \subseteq \mathfrak m_R$) with $\iota(\varpi) = 1 - \zeta$.
--
--   This packages the standard arithmetic of the $q$-th cyclotomic field at the unique prime above $q$ — the ring $\mathbb Z[\zeta_q]$ localised at $(1-\zeta_q)$, with uniformiser $1-\zeta_q$ satisfying $(1-\zeta_q)^{q-1} \sim q$ and residue field $\mathbb F_q$ — as a discrete valuation ring mapping locally into any given characteristic-zero local domain containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity. It is used to supply such a coefficient ring in the analysis of quotients of adic completions of full-level modular curves by the ideal generated by $1 - \zeta$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsPrimitiveRoot_exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_ringHom_pow_sub_one_eq_mul_of_charP_residueField.lean

